I always ditch the quarterstaff as soon as I find my first dagger. You 
should pick up EVERY dagger you find, and throw them as often as you 
possibly can, keeping one for melee an backup. I usually throw all my 
daggers before I start force bolting. You'll level up in daggers quickly 
with this approach and it should help you avoid melee more often.

Other than that, keep your good buddy Elbereth close by. If a monster 
gets a chance to hit you, you probably should've Elberethed two turns ago.

